{"title":"2017 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(detailed_explanation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (detailed explanation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3(_similar_to_solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3( similar to solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> be a 6-digit positive integer, such as 247247, whose first three digits are the same as its last three digits taken in the same order. Which of the following numbers must also be a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc8813f641753b64f8646504d531f48c0a820974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }11\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }19\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }101\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }111\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }1111$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"434\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28detailed_explanation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(detailed_explanation)\">Solution 1 (detailed explanation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (detailed explanation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To check, if a number is divisible by 19, take its unit digit and multiply it by 2, then add the result to the rest of the number, and repeat this step until the number is reduced to two digits. If the result is divisible by 19, then the original number is also divisible by 19.\n</p><p>After we got 19 eliminated, we can see that the other options have a lot of 1's in them. The divisibility rule for 11 is add alternating digits up, then take the difference of them. The example number works like that. If we add variables, ABCDEF to make number ABCABC, we can see that (A+C+B) - (B+A+C) = 0. Which is divisible by 11, so our answer choice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/5647042508b95faacd791a813ecd46df903de1f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>by: CHECKMATE2021 (edited by CHECKMATE2021)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given one of the numbers that can represent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />, so we can just try out the options to see which one is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a7d4bd51ac97209f0eeff1198fc59acef2c66e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$247247$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" />. By the previous solution, 19 does not work even though it is a factor of the example number. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/5647042508b95faacd791a813ecd46df903de1f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~CHECKMATE2021\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3.28_similar_to_solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3(_similar_to_solution_1)\">Solution 3( similar to solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3( similar to solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to solution 1, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/473d198ef2127324c5170a8fecea44e33233f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z=ABCABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"14\" />. To prove it is divisible by 11, we can compute its alternating sum, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/1/b21073514c52e669caa2e81c51c61966f0153956.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A-B+C-A+B-C=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"232\" height=\"16\" />, which is divisible by 11. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/5647042508b95faacd791a813ecd46df903de1f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~PEKKA\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can find that all numbers like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> are divisible by 1001. 1001 is 7 x 11 x 13 and when we divide 11, we get a whole number. So, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/5647042508b95faacd791a813ecd46df903de1f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />. \n</p><p>~AfterglowBlaziken\n</p><p>~Edited by Geometry1421\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/WVHPSVOXE4I\">https://youtu.be/WVHPSVOXE4I</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/At4w8uylvv8?t=99\">https://youtu.be/At4w8uylvv8?t=99</a>\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7an5wU9Q5hk?t=647\">https://youtu.be/7an5wU9Q5hk?t=647</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/-saKu3lLU0U\">https://youtu.be/-saKu3lLU0U</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=